      "writtenOn": "2026-04-22T20:31:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So a real question here - is there really any value to hashing the full IPv6 address? If we just hashed the last 4 bytes, the hash of an IPv4 address and it\u0027s IPv6 encapsulated form would be the same. For other IPv6 addresses, last 4 bytes should be plenty unique for hashing.",
      "revId": "7eb00e86361bc22442b6ed479c84acf14ac3894e",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1dbc7c7_7488ca54",
        "filename": "src/support/ip_utils.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-30T13:14:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can hash only the last 4 bytes as you suggest, but it is basically ignoring the network prefix for IPv6 and potentially increasing the collision range\n\nThe hash that we are doing here is just xoring the 4 words composing the IPv6, so it should be relatively cheap to do",
      "parentUuid": "0b4c75c8_81c5f7c7",
      "revId": "7eb00e86361bc22442b6ed479c84acf14ac3894e",
